          "name": "file_claim_flow",
          "description": "File a Critical Illness or Income Protection claim on one of the verified member's policies. Pass the policy_id from get_my_policies, the claim_type (CriticalIllness or IncomeProtection), the member's own description of what happened, and the documents_needed list from the claim intake step (or empty). The system checks that the policy is Active, that the claim type matches the policy and that no claim is already open on it, then returns FILED with claim_id, the claim-decision case_id, team and reply time, or BLOCKED with a reason. A claims examiner decides every claim - never promise or predict payment. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
          "schemas": {
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://file_claim_Args"
            },
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "open_service_case",
            "handlerDescription": "Hand a request that needs a person to the right team. request_type is beneficiary_change (reference_id = the policy_id, if known), claim_appeal (reference_id = the denied claim_id; agent_brief = the appeal summary), withdrawal_rollover (reference_id = the account_id; amount = dollars or ALL), investment_advice, or complaint. summary is a neutral 1-3 sentence summary in the member's own words. Leave reference_id, amount and agent_brief empty when they do not apply. The system routes it and returns OPENED with case_id, team and reply time, EXISTING, or BLOCKED / INVALID_TYPE with a reason. The assistant never decides, promises or predicts the outcome. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
